hubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T15:41:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T15:41:15Z","body":"I also just tested this on 4.7.beta4 (had to try it locally, since web editor [doesn't work on 4.7.beta3~4](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/76757#issuecomment-4583233012)) and it seems to be banning functions, etc.\r\nI'm glad it's also banning floats in the preprocessor (though bool is still supported, unlike GLSL?).\r\n\r\nAnyway, sorry if this is wrong place for this (dunno if it was reported before) but...\r\n@Chaosus While testing, I noticed the preprocessor include/exclude coloring has a delay, i.e. you gotta type an extra character for it to update this \"gray or color\" effect. And it's updated to whatever was the text before you typed the character.\r\n\r\nIt's easy to test this, e.g.:\r\n```gdshader\r\nshader_type canvas_item;\r\n\r\n#define one 1\r\n#if one == 0\r\nconst int x = 0;\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\nOn the line `#if one == 0` keep changing between 0 and 1, wait a bit, and see that exclusion coloring doesn't match until you type an extra character e.g. space; it matches the previously typed text instead!","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"http